source: crates/zeff-launcher/tests/switch.rs
expression: out
---
----- no version [exit 1]
error: `zeff engine use` takes one version, as `zeff engine use 0.9.1`

run `zeff help` to see the commands

----- a series [exit 1]
error: `0.9` is not the version of an engine: three numbers, as 0.9.1

run `zeff help` to see the commands

----- the engine the project pins [exit 0]
the project already runs on Zeff 0.9.0

----- an engine that is not installed [exit 4]
error[Z0710]: Zeff 0.9.7 is not installed
  = help: `zeff engine use` runs the project on both engines; `zeff engine install 0.9.7` installs it; installed: 0.9.0, 0.9.1

----- outside a project [exit 1]
error[Z0709]: not inside a Zeff project
  = help: `zeff engine use` moves a project to another engine: run it in the project's folder, or name the folder with `-p`

----- the pinned engine is not installed [exit 4]
error[Z0710]: Zeff 0.9.0 is not installed
  = help: `zeff engine use` runs the project on both engines; `zeff engine install 0.9.0` installs it; installed: 0.9.1

----- a project that pins nothing [exit 1]
error: `<tmp>/study/zeff.toml` pins no engine that can be read; `zeff check` says what is wrong with it

run `zeff help` to see the commands
